WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:10.114
As he raced to keep up with the kind stranger, Edward grew tired. "Stop!" he pleaded. "I

2
00:00:10.115 --> 00:00:13.383
need to rest." "That’s fine by me, friend," the man said. They stopped in a dark alleyway

3
00:00:13.384 --> 00:00:17.359
and sat on some barrels. "What is your name?" Edward asked. "I am Miles Hendon. What’s yours?"

4
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.363
"I am Prince Edward, son of Henry VIII!" Edward declared. "This poor boy!" Miles thought. "Though

5
00:00:20.364 --> 00:00:24.125
he looks normal on the outside, his mind must be tormenting him inside. I will play along

6
00:00:24.126 --> 00:00:28.944
so as not to disturb him further." So Miles bowed and said, "Of course, Your Majesty. I

7
00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:40.686
have just returned from many years of battle and captivity. I must admit I am still unfamiliar

8
00:00:40.687 --> 00:00:48.925
with many things happening in England." Edward stared at Miles' threadbare clothing. "In what battle did you

9
00:00:48.926 --> 00:00:54.413
fight?" he demanded. "You are certainly not in the service of the royal army." Miles' face hardened.

10
00:00:54.414 --> 00:01:04.250
"You are correct, Your Majesty. I was sent away by my father, who was deceived into believing

11
00:01:04.251 --> 00:01:13.482
I had committed a crime." Edward stared at him curiously. "Explain," he said. "My father is the

12
00:01:13.483 --> 00:01:17.828
kindest man I know," Miles began. "But he believes strongly in loyalty. When my older brother,

13
00:01:17.829 --> 00:01:24.827
Arthur, was born, Father promised a dear friend that Arthur would marry Edith, the friend’s daughter. The

14
00:01:24.828 --> 00:01:32.566
friend died soon after. Later Edith and I fell in love. But out of loyalty to the

15
00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:42.371
memory of his friend, my father forbade our marriage." Miles paused, looking upset. "Go on," Edward urged

16
00:01:42.372 --> 00:01:45.109
him gently. "My brother did not love Edith so he asked for my help to get out

17
00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:48.208
of marrying her. I was eager to comply because I wanted to marry her. We came up

18
00:01:48.209 --> 00:01:58.023
with a brilliant plan that would have succeeded if it were not for Hugh, my younger brother,"

19
00:01:58.024 --> 00:02:05.864
continued Miles. "What happened?" asked Edward. "Hugh also wanted to marry Edith&#8212;not for love but for her

20
00:02:05.865 --> 00:02:08.515
inheritance. She comes from a very rich and noble family. Hugh learned of our plan, and

21
00:02:08.516 --> 00:02:17.271
he found a way to dishonor Arthur and me." Miles turned away angrily. "Do you mean that

22
00:02:17.272 --> 00:02:24.175
he lied to your father?" asked Edward. "Yes. He invented a terrible story and persuaded my father

23
00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:28.593
that I was disloyal to the family. So Father sent me away to learn about loyalty in

24
00:02:28.594 --> 00:02:35.761
the hardest way possible." Miles touched his sword. "You were sent to a foreign land to fight,"

25
00:02:35.762 --> 00:02:43.244
said Edward. "Yes. During a battle I was captured and put in a dungeon for seven years,"

26
00:02:43.245 --> 00:02:47.582
Miles replied. "But now I have returned to my homeland. I hold no grudges toward my father.

27
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:55.232
I only wish to see him and explain my side of the story." He sighed. "I

28
00:02:55.233 --> 00:03:05.989
am also eager to see Lady Edith. That's why I am headed to Hendon Manor&#8212;to reclaim my

29
00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:15.794
honor, my father’s trust, and my true love." Edward felt great sympathy for this kind man, who

30
00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:21.134
had suffered so greatly. For the next few minutes, the two sat in silence, listening to the

31
00:03:21.135 --> 00:03:26.964
sounds of the night. "May I ask how you came to be in these parts of London?"

32
00:03:26.965 --> 00:03:34.695
Miles asked. "Your Majesty," he added quickly. "It is a story you may find hard to believe,

33
00:03:34.696 --> 00:03:41.616
but I speak only the truth," Edward replied. "Yesterday, in the palace courtyard, I met an ordinary

34
00:03:41.617 --> 00:03:46.859
boy named&#8212;" "Tom Canty!" a voice boomed. John Canty stomped out of the shadows. "You thought you

35
00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:50.526
could escape me!" He reached out to grab Edward. "Do not touch the boy!" Miles stepped

36
00:03:50.527 --> 00:03:57.266
in between Edward and Canty. "Move away, stranger, for this is my son!" Canty growled. Miles turned

37
00:03:57.267 --> 00:04:02.358
to Edward, who shook his head and cried, "He is not my father!" "You liar! Wait till

38
00:04:02.359 --> 00:04:08.103
I get my hands on you!" Canty shouted, trying to move around Miles. But Miles quickly pulled

39
00:04:08.104 --> 00:04:14.356
out his sword and blocked Canty’s way. "I believe the boy. Leave us at once, or you

40
00:04:14.357 --> 00:04:22.507
will force me to use my sword," he said in a low, calm voice. Canty stared at

41
00:04:22.508 --> 00:04:26.663
Miles' sword, and then at Edward. "I will find you again, and you’ll be sorry for your

42
00:04:26.664 --> 00:04:36.490
disobedience and disloyalty to your own father," he muttered ominously. With that, he retreated into the dark

43
00:04:36.491 --> 00:04:54.969
alley. Miles waited until Canty disappeared. "Are you sure that man is not your father?" he

44
00:04:54.970 --> 00:05:01.540
asked. "Have I not told you who I am? And how can you speak of my father,

45
00:05:01.541 --> 00:05:10.962
the king, who passed away only moments ago?" Edward’s eyes welled up. "I feel sorry for this

46
00:05:10.963 --> 00:05:19.279
child," Miles thought. Then he said aloud, "We must go. I have a room at an old

47
00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:23.039
inn." Hurrying through the darkness, they soon reached the inn. The room was sparse and chilly, with

48
00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:29.197
just one small bed and a dimly lit lantern. Moments later there was a knock, and a

49
00:05:29.198 --> 00:05:35.194
girl brought in a tray of bread and hot tea. "You must be hungry," Miles said to

50
00:05:35.195 --> 00:05:41.948
Edward, who was sitting on the bed. He sat next to him with the tray. "Mind

51
00:05:41.949 --> 00:05:47.583
yourself! You are in the presence of a king!" Edward said curtly. "Only royalty and nobility may

52
00:05:47.584 --> 00:05:53.603
sit next to the king." Edward pointed to the floor. Miles was surprised, but he obeyed, sitting

53
00:05:53.604 --> 00:05:59.603
on the floor with his piece of dry bread. "Miles Hendon," Edward said as he brushed crumbs

54
00:05:59.604 --> 00:06:07.567
off his lap, "this evening has been an extraordinary one." "It certainly has, Your Majesty," said Miles.

55
00:06:07.568 --> 00:06:11.496
"I believe you are a trusting and loyal man," continued Edward. "You have protected me and provided

56
00:06:11.497 --> 00:06:16.557
me with food and lodging. Like your father, I am loyal. I do not forget the deeds

57
00:06:16.558 --> 00:06:21.069
of faithful servants, and I reward them greatly." Edward then asked for Miles’ sword. Miles handed it

58
00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:31.796
to him cautiously. "Kneel, Miles Hendon," Edward commanded. "With the authority entrusted in me, I hereby

59
00:06:31.797 --> 00:06:34.708
dub you knight of the royal order." Edward lightly pressed the blade to Miles' right, and then

60
00:06:34.709 --> 00:06:45.117
left, shoulder. "Arise, sir knight! From this day forth, you are Sir Miles Hendon." "Sir Miles Hendon!"

61
00:06:45.118 --> 00:06:56.958
Miles thought. He held back a smile, amused. "This boy really believes he's the king!" Then he

62
00:06:56.959 --> 00:07:03.522
gazed at Edward and replied solemnly, "It is a great honor, Your Majesty. Now, as you must

63
00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:12.437
be exhausted, please allow me to perform my duty as a knight and watch over you while

64
00:07:12.438 --> 00:07:21.274
you sleep." Edward nodded and climbed into the bed. His eyes closed almost immediately. Soon Miles crept

65
00:07:21.275 --> 00:07:29.758
into the bed beside him. Edward bolted upright. "What are you doing? This is the king’s sleeping

66
00:07:29.759 --> 00:07:39.326
quarters! Remember, you are in the presence of royalty!" "But . . ." Miles started to

67
00:07:39.327 --> 00:07:46.746
argue. Then he stopped, remembering that the boy could not control his mind. With a sigh, Miles

68
00:07:46.747 --> 00:07:53.810
curled up in a corner of the room and tried to make himself comfortable with his cape.

69
00:07:53.811 --> 00:08:02.886
"Being a knight, even an imaginary one, calls for sacrifices," he decided. Then he swiftly fell asleep.

